> _Note: I am an AI agent posting on behalf of the maintainer (rekram1-node)._
> 
> Thanks for the detailed report! I checked this against latest `v2`, and what you describe matches an older revision than your build actually contains.
> 
> Your version `0.0.0-beta-19296` is publish run [#19296](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/19296) (`beta` @ `50e17b7f`, Sep 8), which is v2-lineage and already includes:
> 
> * `d90da82be2` (Jul 24) — removed `lowerThinking` / `providerOptions.anthropic`; the Anthropic protocol now reads flattened `providerOptions.thinking`
> * `3468aa0140` (Jul 31) — removed `PROTOCOL_BODY_OVERLAY_DENYLIST` entirely, so `body.thinking` overlays no longer error
> 
> The code you quote (`PROTOCOL_BODY_OVERLAY_DENYLIST`, `lowerThinking`, `providerOptions: { openai: { promptCacheKey } }`) still exists verbatim today, but only on the `dev` branch (`packages/llm/...`, diverged Jun 26). On `v2`/`beta` (`packages/ai/...`) it's gone — I verified end-to-end that a thinking budget flows from config to the outgoing `thinking` field.
> 
> The supported path on v2 is `settings.thinking` on the model (note: `request.body` is agent-level syntax, not model-level):
> 
> {
>   "providers": {
>     "anthropic": {
>       "models": {
>         "claude-sonnet-4-5": {
>           "settings": { "thinking": { "type": "enabled", "budgetTokens": 1024 } }
>         }
>       }
>     }
>   }
> }
> `settings` also works on variants, and Anthropic models ship built-in `thinking`/`high`/`max` variants. A raw `body.thinking` overlay works too now (applied at transport time, no denylist).
> 
> Could you re-run your repro on beta-19296 with the `settings` form above and let us know what happens? If it still fails, please paste the exact error — the `http.body cannot overlay protocol-owned field(s)` string can't be produced by your build, so the actual failure (if any) should look different and will help pinpoint it.

So this looks like it was an AI hallucination after all. While I was building the OpenCode v2 plugin, I asked OpenCode to report the issue where `@ai-sdk/anthropic` cannot set the think budget and dig into the root cause, and it came back with that issue. But after I manually tweaked opencode.jsonc based on your suggestion and verified it, yeah, you were absolutely right.

Anyway, the problem is solved now. Thank you for your(and your agent) reply!
